# Experiment D: query load at four concurrency levels (1, 8, 24, 48 clients, 480 s each, then 900 s
# with no client so the services can scale in) on tier S data, decision P15-1. Phase 15 Wave 2.
# UNAPPROVED and UNEXECUTED. Format: scripts/README.md, "Experiment manifest contract".
# No spaces in values. The design is in load-tests/query-load/README.md (it supersedes the old
# levels 1, 4, 8, 16 of load-tests/README.md).
# PLACEHOLDERS the human replaces before an approval record is written
# (the record binds the sha256 of the final file, so any edit needs a new record):
#   ACCOUNT_ID       123456789012 is the documented example, not a real account.
#   (DATASET_SNAPSHOT is filled: scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b, reported by WO-4 and
#                    verified by the human.)
#   OUTPUT_ROOT      /abs/outside/repo/... is a placeholder path; pick a durable directory
#                    outside the repository.
# Limits (tier S caps of decision P15-1: 90 min, 64 clients, 20000 tasks):
#   MAX_CONCURRENCY 48  the top level (was 16). Within the 64 cap.
#   MAX_TASKS 20000     the request bound of the committed schedule is 19,521 =
#                       (1 + 8 + 24 + 48) x (floor(480 / 2.0) + 1) with think time 2.0 to 4.0 s; the
#                       client enforces the bound at run time (exit 3 at a cap). Expected about
#                       11,100 requests at 0.5 s latency. At the cap.
#   MAX_MINUTES 70      the schedule takes 47 min (4 x 8 + 15); run.sh gives the client MAX_MINUTES
#                       minus 15 and requires at least 50, so 65 is the least; 70 leaves 5 min of
#                       slack. Within the 90 cap.
# Uses the offline stub answer model (P15-4): no Bedrock charge.
# COST (HOURLY_BURN_USD and SPEND_CEILING_USD): session 2 values from WO-10, infra/terraform/COST_ESTIMATE.md,
# section "Session 2 (services) hourly burn and HIGH", paragraph "Provisional experiment burns".
# HOURLY_BURN_USD 0.55 = steady 0.37 + 3 extra query tasks 0.114 + load client 0.049, rounded up.
# Was 0.85 (tier M draft).
# SPEND_CEILING_USD 0.65: 0.55 x 70 min / 60 = 0.6417, under the ceiling 0.65 (0.0083 headroom,
# the document's own rounding). Was 1.50. The burn covers the experiment hours only; the offline stub
# answer model has no Bedrock charge, and the S3 Vectors queries (2.50 USD per million) are cents.
# CAVEAT for the human: every rate behind the 0.37 steady burn is UNVERIFIED (memory; only the
# Fargate per-second rates are read anchors), so the value is the WO-10 figure, not a verified rate.
MANIFEST_VERSION=1
EXPERIMENT_ID=D
DESCRIPTION=query-load-four-levels-1-8-24-48-clients-480s-each-then-900s-idle-tier-s
ENVIRONMENT=course
REGION=us-east-2
ACCOUNT_ID=123456789012
DATASET_SNAPSHOT=scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b
SIZE_TIER=S
MAX_MINUTES=70
MAX_CONCURRENCY=48
MAX_TASKS=20000
SPEND_CEILING_USD=0.65
HOURLY_BURN_USD=0.55
STOP_CONDITIONS=wall-clock,first-failure,spend-estimate
METRIC_NAMES=TargetResponseTime,RequestCount,HTTPCode_Target_5XX_Count,HTTPCode_ELB_5XX_Count,HealthyHostCount,DesiredTaskCount,RunningTaskCount,CPUUtilization,MemoryUtilization,MainRequestQueuePendingRequests,ReadThrottleEvents,WriteThrottleEvents,ConsumedReadCapacityUnits,ConsumedWriteCapacityUnits
METRIC_NAMESPACES=AWS/ApplicationELB,ECS/ContainerInsights,AWS/ECS,AWS/DynamoDB,AWS/Neptune
OUTPUT_ROOT=/abs/outside/repo/scholarchain-experiments
ENTRY_POINT=script:experiments/d-query-load/run.sh
